Z||000005||John E. Rowlett||11-01-2001||09:49 AM||||Ny knowledge of the Fiero is limited but my Fiero is a 85 GT 4 speed and all factory. I assume my tranny is stock. I build drag cars and have been mechanican for years. This problem does not seem to be syncros as there is no grinding on down **** . I will try new oil as suggested. Possibly someone can give me a walk thru on adjusting linkage/shifter?||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||11-01-2001||09:56 AM||||Maybe the clutch isn't fully disengaging.  I had a similar problem.  shifting at higher rpm's would grind the gears shifting into second.  I suppose that means it's not going in, properly any how.  My clutch fork was forked up and destroyed everything else when it finally failed.  I thought I had a  tranny with bad syncro's until it failed.  either way I wasn't happy.  OK, I was extremely pissed off. Still am over the money put into that system in the last year.  It's fixed correctly now.||||reg||1
